# Archived — Content migrated to `design/03_world/LATTICE_DOCTRINE.md`

**Status:** superseded / archived  
**Migrated to:** `design/03_world/LATTICE_DOCTRINE.md`  

This was a raw conversation dump. The content has been formalized into a proper design document. See the new location for the authoritative version.

---

Perfect. That actually makes the entire concept click into place.

The worlds being temporary means:

# the Archives are not saving the world permanently.

They are:

> inflating survivable reality pockets for a limited duration.

That is MUCH more tragic and much more mechanically useful.

It also solves a massive design problem:
you now have a canonical explanation for:

- campaign resets
- seasonal worlds
- procgen instability
- extraction loops
- temporary settlements
- shifting sectors
- failed colonies
- disappearing maps

without handwaving.

---

# The New Structure

## Campaign Worlds Are “Stabilization Bubbles”

Each campaign is:

- a temporary continuity pocket
- inflated by an Archive engine
- barely insulated from total erasure

The Archive can only:

- hold so much territory
- sustain coherence temporarily
- resist collapse for a finite duration

Eventually:

# the pressure outside wins.

The bubble fails.

The world collapses.

---

# This Is NOT A Planet

Very important distinction.

Do NOT make campaigns entire planets.

They should feel like:

- isolated surviving sectors
- continuity pockets
- fractured territorial remnants
- temporary stitched-together reality zones

The edges of the world should feel:
wrong.

---

# The Boundary

One of the coolest things you can do:

Never use:

- invisible walls
- map borders
- radiation zones

Instead:

# the world simply stops existing.

At the outer edge:

- geometry truncates
- lighting collapses
- sound dampens
- stars disappear
- terrain phases into impossible static absence
- distant structures are half-erased

Maybe:
objects near the edge:

- lose textures
- lose names
- lose collision
- partially disappear frame-to-frame

That is horrifying.

---

# What Archive Completion Actually Means

You are not “winning the world.”

You are:

# extending the lifespan of the bubble.

